# Person Avatar (冻结)

Deterministic **initial + colored circle** avatars for person names. Do not duplicate hash/color logic or hardcode palette elsewhere.

## Single source of truth

| Concern | File |
|---------|------|
| Hash + palette + name parsing | `src/personAvatar/personAvatar.ts` |
| Avatar UI | `src/personAvatar/PersonAvatar.vue` |
| Avatar styles | `src/personAvatar/PersonAvatar.module.css` |
| Public API | `src/personAvatar/index.ts` |

## Usage

```ts
import { PersonAvatar, getAvatarColor, getPersonInitial, parsePersonList } from '@/personAvatar';
```

```html
<PersonAvatar name="EDS Yang" />
```

Multi-person row (e.g. DocMetaPanel 维护/贡献):

```html
<span v-for="name in parsePersonList(value)" :key="name">
  <PersonAvatar :name="name" />
  <span>{{ name }}</span>
</span>
```

## Color (frozen)

- Palette: Figma **web3-avatar-1…20**
- Selection: `(hashString(name) + paletteOffset) % 20` — same hash as [avatar-gen-js](https://github.com/kohaiy/avatar-gen-js/)
- Same name → same color (deterministic); multi-person rows add `paletteOffset` (list index)
- Green-family palette slots (indices 1, 4, 8, 11, 13) are skipped — walk to next non-green slot
- `EDS Yang` ↔ `Dev.` use each other's hashed palette color (offset 0 / 1)

## Initial (frozen)

- Strip trailing `.`, take **last word** first letter, uppercase
- `EDS Yang` → `Y`; `Jojo` → `J`; `Dev.` → `D`

## Avatar chrome (frozen)

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Size | 16×16px |
| Shape | `border-radius: var(--radius-full)` (squircle via global corner-smoothing) |
| Background | inline `backgroundColor` from `getAvatarColor(name)` |
| Text color | `var(--text-same-white-primary)` |
| Font | `var(--font-family-text)`, **16px rendered at scale(0.5)** → ~8px visual, weight **600**, line-height 1 |
| Crisp small type | Inner `.initial` at 2× size + `transform: scale(0.5)`; `-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased` |

## Person list layout (DocMetaPanel)

- Fields: **维护**, **贡献** only
- Separator: none — use `gap: var(--spacing-1)` on `.personList`
- Avatar ↔ name gap: `var(--spacing-05)` on `.person`
- Value font: global `var(--font-family-text)` (not IBM Plex Mono)

## When adding avatars elsewhere

1. Import `PersonAvatar` from `@/personAvatar` — do not copy SVG/CSS
2. New palette entries: update `WEB3_AVATAR_COLORS` in `personAvatar.ts` + this rule
3. Different size: extend `PersonAvatar` with a `size` prop — do not fork a second avatar component
